# What Vercel does NOT upload to the build.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE USES .gitignore SYNTAX. A pattern with no leading slash matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. That is the whole reason every docs-ish
# line below is anchored with `/`: an unanchored `docs` would also match
# `public/docs`, which is THE ENTIRE FROZEN LEGACY SITE — 15 HTML pages, both
# PDFs, the images, the css and the js, every one of them a live URL that is on
# a résumé and on LinkedIn. It would deploy green and 404 the résumé.
# (Addendum B, ruling R-11.)
#
# ⚠ The previous version of this file excluded `docs/images` and `docs/*.pdf`,
# on the written premise that "the portfolio site itself is served by GitHub
# Pages". That premise expires at the DNS cutover. Re-adding either line 404s
# /docs/Resume.pdf and the portrait on the live domain the moment DNS moves.
# Verified 2026-09-02: Resume.pdf is 200 on duyng-portfolio.com and 404 on
# seattle-university-portfolio.vercel.app today, because of exactly those lines.

# ── Archived subtrees: in git for history, never in a build ──────────────────
/second-brain
/ml-demos
/notebook
/presentation
/documentation
/duy-portfolio-mcp

# Root images/ is a byte-identical duplicate of public/docs/images/ and is
# referenced by nothing. Orphaned, kept on disk, excluded from the build.
/images

# ── Engineering documents ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANCHORED. This is the root docs/ folder (specs, ADRs, design notes), NOT
# public/docs. If this line ever loses its leading slash the legacy site
# disappears from production.
/docs

# ── Private working files that must never be published ──────────────────────
# Jekyll silently 404s dot-directories; Next.js SERVES them out of public/
# (measured on next@16.3.4). next.config.ts rewrites the path to a 404 and
# scripts/verify-urls.sh asserts it, but the cheapest guarantee is for the bytes
# never to leave this machine.
/public/docs/.claude

# Finder metadata. UNANCHORED on purpose — every depth, unlike the docs-ish
# lines above. `.gitignore` already excludes these, so a git-driven deploy never
# sees them; a `vercel deploy` from a working tree honours THIS file and not
# `.gitignore`, and four of them exist under public/ on the maintainer's machine
# today (public/, public/docs/, public/docs/css/, public/docs/images/). A
# .DS_Store is a directory listing: it names every file beside it, including any
# that were deleted from the site but not from the folder.
# Measured on next@16.3.4: /docs/.DS_Store returns 500, not 404 — Next declines
# to serve it but does not pretend it is absent.
.DS_Store

# ── Repo and dev tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.github
/.claude
/backend/tests
/backend/scripts
/backend/dependencies
/tests
/playwright.config.ts
/vitest.config.ts

# ── Retired Python modules: kept in-tree, never deployed ─────────────────────
# POST /chat is RETIRED, not ported (Addendum B, ruling R-3). Nothing that
# Vercel loads imports any of these, and none of them belongs in a function
# bundle. api/index.py mounts the evaluation blueprint and nothing else.
/backend/src/app.py
/backend/src/agent.py
/backend/src/chatservice.py
/backend/src/llm.py
/backend/src/tools

# ── Stale GitHub Pages / Render artifacts ────────────────────────────────────
# CNAME and _config.yml are DELETED at the cutover, not before — deleting either
# while DNS still points at GitHub Pages breaks the live site. Until then they
# are simply not uploaded. See RUNBOOK-cutover.md.
/render.yaml
/_config.yml
/CNAME
/index.html
/LICENSE
